# Local MQTT broker settings for the TheLink firmware.
#
# This file is an example. The real one is sdkconfig.secrets, which is
# gitignored and is rewritten by every `python3 scripts/build.py` run. You
# normally do not need to create it at all - the build asks for the values and
# writes the file for you.
#
# The format is Kconfig: these become CONFIG_BROKER_URL, CONFIG_MQTT_USERNAME
# and CONFIG_MQTT_PASSWORD in the firmware. CONFIG_BROKER_URL is a normal
# menuconfig option too - the build prompt can override it, but it only writes
# it here when you actually type one, so menuconfig keeps ownership of it.
#
# A field that is missing from this file is not set by this file: it falls back
# to menuconfig (and an empty username means the firmware connects
# anonymously, which is what an unauthenticated public broker expects).
#
# The values are also embedded in build*/sdkconfig and in the firmware image,
# so treat the built binary as sensitive.
CONFIG_BROKER_URL="mqtt://broker.emqx.io"
CONFIG_MQTT_USERNAME=""
CONFIG_MQTT_PASSWORD=""
